{"status": "success", "data": [{"site": {"area": 22505.20099258423, "notes": "In Neotoma, previously called \"Site 24 (Whitehead and Jackson 1990)\" for a pollen surface sample.                                                    Lake is perched in a glacial-scoured bedrock basin with a bedrock outlet spillway.  The west side of the basin is ocupied by a sedge/Sphagnum peatland.  The lake is spring-fed, with rivulets entering the peatland on the north and west sides from steep slopes above.    Surrounding forests are dominated by Abies balsamea, with Betula papyrifera var. cordifolia and Picea mariana.  All three species grow along the lakeshore.  Forests on adjacent slopes are primarily Abies and Betula, with classic 'fir wave' patterns.  Only aquatic species observed in the lake are Potamogeton confervoides, Sphagnum sp., and sterile Sparganium (probably S. angustifolia) (Jackson & Charles 1988, Canad. J. Bot. 66:1449-1460).", "siteid": 734, "dataset": {"doi": ["10.21233/n3ss4m", "10.21233/n3ct5m"], "agerange": [{"units": null, "ageold": null, "ageyoung": null}], "database": "North American Pollen Database", "datasetid": 754, "datasetpi": [{"initials": "D.R.", "contactid": 109, "firstname": "Donald R.", "familyname": "Whitehead", "contactname": "Whitehead, Donald R."}], "datasetname": "DRW032", "datasettype": "pollen surface sample", "datasetnotes": null}, "altitude": 1317, "sitename": "Lake Tear of the Clouds", "geography": "{\"type\":\"Polygon\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[[[-73.93672,44.10645],[-73.93394,44.10645],[-73.93394,44.10736],[-73.93672,44.10736],[-73.93672,44.10645]]]}", "geopolitical": ["United States", "New York", "Essex", "Adirondack Park"], "collectionunit": {"notes": null, "handle": "TEAR_C90", "colldate": "1979-01-01", "location": "Deepest area in lake", "waterdepth": null, "gpslocation": {"gpserror": null, "latitude": null, "longitude": null, "gpsaltitude": null}, "collunittype": "Modern",